{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:FluidDynamics.NsRegularQou","@type":"LeanModule","name":"FluidDynamics.NsRegularQou","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:NSRegularQOU.not_isNSRegular_iff_isNSSingular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSRegularQOU.not_isNSRegular_iff_isNSSingular","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-regular-qou.lean#L51-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSRegularQOU.isNSSingular_iff_chi_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSRegularQOU.isNSSingular_iff_chi_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-regular-qou.lean#L48-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSRegularQOU.isNSRegular_iff_chi_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSRegularQOU.isNSRegular_iff_chi_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-regular-qou.lean#L45-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSRegularQOU.IsNSSingular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSRegularQOU.IsNSSingular","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-regular-qou.lean#L42-L43","doc":"Categorical NS-singularity label: the global Euler class is non-zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSRegularQOU.IsNSRegular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSRegularQOU.IsNSRegular","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-regular-qou.lean#L39-L40","doc":"Categorical NS-regularity label: the global Euler class vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSRegularQOU.nsObstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSRegularQOU.nsObstruction","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-regular-qou.lean#L35-L37","doc":"The global surface NS obstruction `NS(A) := e(ξ) ∈ H²(S, ℤ) ≅ ℤ`,\nidentified with its degree `χ(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSRegularQOU.chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSRegularQOU.chi","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-regular-qou.lean#L31-L31","doc":"The Euler characteristic `χ(A) = tr(κ₀) = deg e(ξ)` of the categorical data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSRegularQOU.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSRegularQOU.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-regular-qou.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSRegularQOU.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSRegularQOU.q","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-regular-qou.lean#L28-L28","doc":"Substrate parameter q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSRegularQOU.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSRegularQOU.mk","kind":"ctor","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-regular-qou.lean#L26-L26","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSRegularQOU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSRegularQOU","kind":"structure","line":6,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-regular-qou.lean#L6-L31","doc":"Data of a quantum universe as used by the NS-regularity classification of\nthe sibling `.md`: the substrate parameter `q > 1` and the Euler\ncharacteristic `χ(A) = tr(κ₀) = deg e(ξ)` of the Reeb bundle `ξ` on the\nspectral surface `S`.\n\n**Global surface class (2026-11-15, owner decision Q-VO9T-2 = 1, beans\n`qou-nzyr`, `qou-hjl0`).** An intermediate version defined `NS(A)` as the\nrestriction `κ₀|_Σ ∈ H²(Σ, 𝓑)` to a one-dimensional collision curve `Σ`,\nwhich vanishes identically (`H²(Σ, ·) = 0`, item 3 of\n`thm:ns-singularity-descartes`). Per owner ruling Q-VO9T-2 = 1 (matching\n`QOU.FluidDynamics.qou_ns_in_qou`), `NS(A)` is the **global** surface Euler\nclass `e(ξ) ∈ H²(S, ℤ) ≅ ℤ`, represented by its degree `χ(A)`. Thus\n`IsNSRegular` (`NS(A) = 0`) holds iff `χ(A) = 0`, and `IsNSSingular`\n(`NS(A) ≠ 0`) holds iff `χ(A) ≠ 0`.\n\n**Scope (framework model correspondence).** `IsNSRegular` and `IsNSSingular`\nare internal categorical labels for `e(ξ)` on `S`. They do not assert a\ndeductive theorem about the classical unforced 3D Navier–Stokes PDE on `ℝ³`\nor `𝕋³` (Tao's averaged-NS barrier, J. Amer. Math. Soc. 29 (2016), 601–674;\n`docs/audits/2026-10-12-ns-v3-tao-barrier.md`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}